<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Agentic System Evaluation Related Details</h3>

<section id="A1.SS3.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.3.1 </span>Metrics Details</h4>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Exact Match (EM).</span> provides the strictest evaluation criterion by requiring complete string equality between the predicted value <math id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{\text{pred}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mtext>pred</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{\text{pred}}</annotation></semantics></math> and ground truth <math id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{\text{gt}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mtext>gt</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{\text{gt}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{EM}(v_{\text{gt}},v_{\text{pred}})=\begin{cases}1,&amp;\text{if }v_{\text{gt}}=v_{\text{pred}}\\
0,&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>EM</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mtext>gt</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mtext>pred</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mtext>gt</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mtext>pred</mtext></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>otherwise</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{EM}(v_{\text{gt}},v_{\text{pred}})=\begin{cases}1,&amp;\text{if }v_{\text{gt}}=v_{\text{pred}}\\
0,&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This metric is particularly important for structured fields such as declaration numbers, product codes, where even a single character deviation renders the prediction unusable. Many such fields in DoP documents follow rigid templates and should be reproduced verbatim.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">BLEU Score (with smoothing).</span> measures the <math id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-gram precision between the predicted value <math id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{\text{pred}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mtext>pred</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{\text{pred}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the reference <math id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{\text{gt}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mtext>gt</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{\text{gt}}</annotation></semantics></math>. It is effective for short to medium-length technical descriptions. Though originally designed for machine translation, it rewards overlapping lexical fragments even if their order varies, we compute it as:</p>
<table id="A1.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{BLEU}(v_{\text{gt}},v_{\text{pred}})=\exp\left(\sum_{n=1}^{N}w_{n}\cdot\log p_{n}\right)\cdot\text{BP}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>BLEU</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mtext>gt</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mtext>pred</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mtext>BP</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{BLEU}(v_{\text{gt}},v_{\text{pred}})=\exp\left(\sum_{n=1}^{N}w_{n}\cdot\log p_{n}\right)\cdot\text{BP}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is the modified <math id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-gram precision for order <math id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is the weight assigned to each <math id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-gram (typically <math id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{n}=\frac{1}{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{n}=\frac{1}{N}</annotation></semantics></math>), and <span id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">BP</span> denotes the brevity penalty to penalize short predictions. BLEU is computed using NLTK’s sentence-level scorer with up to 4-grams and SmoothingFunction (method 4) to handle cases with low or zero overlap.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">BLEU is helpful in evaluating fields like intended use or assessment systems, where phrasing may differ while retaining technical terminology. However, it is limited in recall and less robust to paraphrasing, which is addressed by ROUGE-L.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">ROUGE-L.</span> measures the similarity between predicted and reference text using the longest common subsequence (LCS). The F1 version of the ROUGE-L score is defined as:</p>
<table id="A1.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{ROUGE-L}(v_{\text{gt}},v_{\text{pred}})=\frac{(1+\beta^{2})\cdot P\cdot R}{R+\beta^{2}\cdot P}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>ROUGE-L</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mtext>gt</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mtext>pred</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{ROUGE-L}(v_{\text{gt}},v_{\text{pred}})=\frac{(1+\beta^{2})\cdot P\cdot R}{R+\beta^{2}\cdot P}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P=\frac{\text{LCS}(v_{\text{gt}},v_{\text{pred}})}{|v_{\text{pred}}|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mtext>LCS</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mtext>gt</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mtext>pred</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mtext>pred</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P=\frac{\text{LCS}(v_{\text{gt}},v_{\text{pred}})}{|v_{\text{pred}}|}</annotation></semantics></math> is the precision, <math id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=\frac{\text{LCS}(v_{\text{gt}},v_{\text{pred}})}{|v_{\text{gt}}|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mtext>LCS</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mtext>gt</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mtext>pred</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mtext>gt</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=\frac{\text{LCS}(v_{\text{gt}},v_{\text{pred}})}{|v_{\text{gt}}|}</annotation></semantics></math> is the recall, and <math id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=1</annotation></semantics></math> balances precision and recall.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">We implement ROUGE-L using the <span id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">rouge-score</span> Python library with stemming enabled. Unlike BLEU, ROUGE-L emphasizes sequence alignment and recall, making it suitable for long, nested fields such as the "Declared Performance" block. It is robust to minor rewordings, reordering, and partial omissions.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F4" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.11773v1/Figures/metric_selection.png" id="A1.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/241;" width="476" height="241" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 4: </span>Agentic Tool Selection and Execution Flow in DoP-ACT</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Each metric reveals different correctness and failure modes. Exact Match enforces binary correctness, essential for identifiers. BLEU captures surface-level lexical overlap in moderately variable phrases. ROUGE-L handles paraphrased, nested, or reordered content in longer fields. For example, a prediction might fail EM due to formatting but still convey equivalent meaning, reflected by a high ROUGE score. BLEU helps distinguish semantically plausible but imprecise outputs from incomplete ones.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">As shown in Figure <a href="#A1.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ A.3.1 Metrics Details ‣ A.3 Agentic System Evaluation Related Details ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ An Agentic Toolkit for Adaptive Information Extraction from Regulatory Documents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, the combined use of EM, BLEU, and ROUGE-L ensures robust coverage across content types, ranging from atomic identifiers to free-text paragraphs, balancing strict correctness with semantic flexibility.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">After computing JSON Validity, Key Match Ratio (see Equations (<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_label ltx_ref_self"></span>),  (<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_label ltx_ref_self"></span>)), and Value Similarity scores (Exact Match, BLEU, and ROUGE-L (see Equations (<a href="#A1.E1" title="In A.3.1 Metrics Details ‣ A.3 Agentic System Evaluation Related Details ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ An Agentic Toolkit for Adaptive Information Extraction from Regulatory Documents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>),  (<a href="#A1.E2" title="In A.3.1 Metrics Details ‣ A.3 Agentic System Evaluation Related Details ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ An Agentic Toolkit for Adaptive Information Extraction from Regulatory Documents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>),  (<a href="#A1.E3" title="In A.3.1 Metrics Details ‣ A.3 Agentic System Evaluation Related Details ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ An Agentic Toolkit for Adaptive Information Extraction from Regulatory Documents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>))), we aggregate results at the document and language levels to enable fair comparison across multilingual DoP documents.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.3.2 </span>Aggregation of Evaluation Metrics for KVP Task</h4>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As described in Algorithm <a href="#algorithm1" title="In A.3.2 Aggregation of Evaluation Metrics for KVP Task ‣ A.3 Agentic System Evaluation Related Details ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ An Agentic Toolkit for Adaptive Information Extraction from Regulatory Documents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, evaluation is conducted on each <math id="A1.SS3.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\text{doc},\text{language})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>doc</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext>language</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\text{doc},\text{language})</annotation></semantics></math> pair, producing five scalar scores. The system is expected to predict values for 12 target keys per document. To ensure this expectation is met and the evaluation is not biased by incomplete predictions, we assign a similarity score of zero for any ground truth key that is missing from the system output. This effectively penalizes omissions. Value similarity metrics (Exact Match, BLEU, ROUGE-L) are computed only on matched keys, and the totals are normalized by <math id="A1.SS3.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max(|\mathcal{M}_{d,\ell}|,\ 12)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn> 12</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max(|\mathcal{M}_{d,\ell}|,\ 12)</annotation></semantics></math> to ensure consistency across varying numbers of matches. After per-sample evaluation, we aggregate results by computing document–language averages, followed by a final macro-average over all documents and languages.</p>
</div>
<figure id="algorithm1" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="algorithm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span>Key-Value Evaluation Procedure for Each Document-Language Pair</figcaption>
<div id="algorithm1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="algorithm1.4.1" class="ltx_listingline">


<span id="algorithm1.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input :</span> Predicted output <math id="algorithm1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{d,\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{d,\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> (JSON string), ground truth <math id="algorithm1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{d,\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{d,\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> (key-value dictionary)
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.2" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output :</span> <math id="algorithm1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{valid}_{d,\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>valid</mtext><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{valid}_{d,\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="algorithm1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{KeyMatch}_{d,\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>KeyMatch</mtext><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{KeyMatch}_{d,\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="algorithm1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{EM}_{d,\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>EM</mtext><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{EM}_{d,\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="algorithm1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{BLEU}_{d,\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>BLEU</mtext><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{BLEU}_{d,\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="algorithm1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{ROUGE}_{d,\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>ROUGE</mtext><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{ROUGE}_{d,\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.3" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1</span></span>
              <span id="algorithm1.4.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 1: JSON Validity Check</span> ;  <span id="algorithm1.4.3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm1.4.3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">See Eq. (<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_label ltx_ref_self"></span>)</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.4" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">2</span></span>
              <span id="algorithm1.4.4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <em id="algorithm1.4.4.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{d,\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{d,\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> can be parsed into a key–value dictionary</em> <span id="algorithm1.4.4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.5" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">3</span></span>
              <math id="algorithm1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{valid}_{d,\ell}\leftarrow 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>valid</mtext><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{valid}_{d,\ell}\leftarrow 1</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.6" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">4</span></span>
              Parse <math id="algorithm1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}_{d,\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}_{d,\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> into dictionary format;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.7" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">5</span></span>
              <span id="algorithm1.4.7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.8" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">6</span></span>
              <math id="algorithm1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{valid}_{d,\ell}\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>valid</mtext><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{valid}_{d,\ell}\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.9" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">7</span></span>
              <span id="algorithm1.4.9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <em id="algorithm1.4.9.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{valid}_{d,\ell},\ 0,\ 0,\ 0,\ 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">valid</mtext><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mn> 0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn> 0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn> 0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{valid}_{d,\ell},\ 0,\ 0,\ 0,\ 0</annotation></semantics></math></em>;  <span id="algorithm1.4.9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm1.4.9.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Skip if invalid JSON</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.10" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">8</span></span>
              <span id="algorithm1.4.10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 2: Key Matching</span> ;  <span id="algorithm1.4.10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm1.4.10.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">See Eq. (<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_label ltx_ref_self"></span>)</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.11" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">9</span></span>
              <math id="algorithm1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\text{gt}}\leftarrow\{k_{i}\mid(k_{i},v_{i}^{\text{gt}})\in\mathcal{G}_{d,\ell}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mtext>gt</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>gt</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\text{gt}}\leftarrow\{k_{i}\mid(k_{i},v_{i}^{\text{gt}})\in\mathcal{G}_{d,\ell}\}</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.12" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.12.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">10</span></span>
              <math id="algorithm1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\text{pred}}\leftarrow\{k_{j}\mid(k_{j},v_{j}^{\text{pred}})\in\mathcal{P}_{d,\ell}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mtext>pred</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi><mtext>pred</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\text{pred}}\leftarrow\{k_{j}\mid(k_{j},v_{j}^{\text{pred}})\in\mathcal{P}_{d,\ell}\}</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.13" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.13.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">11</span></span>
              <math id="algorithm1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{d,\ell}\leftarrow K_{\text{gt}}\cap K_{\text{pred}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mtext>gt</mtext></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mtext>pred</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{d,\ell}\leftarrow K_{\text{gt}}\cap K_{\text{pred}}</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.14" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.14.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">12</span></span>
              <math id="algorithm1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{KeyMatch}_{d,\ell}\leftarrow\frac{|\mathcal{M}_{d,\ell}|}{|K_{\text{gt}}|+\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>KeyMatch</mtext><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mtext>gt</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{KeyMatch}_{d,\ell}\leftarrow\frac{|\mathcal{M}_{d,\ell}|}{|K_{\text{gt}}|+\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>;  <span id="algorithm1.4.14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm1.4.14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Avoid divide-by-zero with <math id="algorithm1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math></span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.15" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.15.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">13</span></span>
              <span id="algorithm1.4.15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 3: Value Similarity Metrics</span> ;  <span id="algorithm1.4.15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm1.4.15.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Compute scores only on matched keys</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.16" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.16.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">14</span></span>
              Initialize: <math id="algorithm1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{EM}_{d,\ell}\leftarrow 0,\ \text{BLEU}_{d,\ell}\leftarrow 0,\ \text{ROUGE}_{d,\ell}\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mtext>EM</mtext><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>BLEU</mtext><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>ROUGE</mtext><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{EM}_{d,\ell}\leftarrow 0,\ \text{BLEU}_{d,\ell}\leftarrow 0,\ \text{ROUGE}_{d,\ell}\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.17" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.17.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">15</span></span>
              <span id="algorithm1.4.17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">foreach</span> <em id="algorithm1.4.17.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\mathcal{M}_{d,\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\mathcal{M}_{d,\ell}</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm1.4.17.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.18" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.18.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">16</span></span>
              Normalize <math id="algorithm1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{k}^{\text{gt}},\ v_{k}^{\text{pred}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi><mtext>gt</mtext></msubsup><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi><mtext>pred</mtext></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{k}^{\text{gt}},\ v_{k}^{\text{pred}}</annotation></semantics></math>;  <span id="algorithm1.4.18.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm1.4.18.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">e.g., lowercasing, punctuation stripping</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.19" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.19.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">17</span></span>
              ;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.20" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.20.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">18</span></span>
              <math id="algorithm1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{EM}_{d,\ell}\leftarrow\text{EM}_{d,\ell}+\text{EM}(v_{k}^{\text{gt}},v_{k}^{\text{pred}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>EM</mtext><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>EM</mtext><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mtext>EM</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi><mtext>gt</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi><mtext>pred</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{EM}_{d,\ell}\leftarrow\text{EM}_{d,\ell}+\text{EM}(v_{k}^{\text{gt}},v_{k}^{\text{pred}})</annotation></semantics></math>;  <span id="algorithm1.4.20.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm1.4.20.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">See Eq. (<a href="#A1.E1" title="In A.3.1 Metrics Details ‣ A.3 Agentic System Evaluation Related Details ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ An Agentic Toolkit for Adaptive Information Extraction from Regulatory Documents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>)</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.21" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.21.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">19</span></span>
              ;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.22" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.22.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">20</span></span>
              <math id="algorithm1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{BLEU}_{d,\ell}\leftarrow\text{BLEU}_{d,\ell}+\text{BLEU}(v_{k}^{\text{gt}},v_{k}^{\text{pred}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>BLEU</mtext><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>BLEU</mtext><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mtext>BLEU</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi><mtext>gt</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi><mtext>pred</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{BLEU}_{d,\ell}\leftarrow\text{BLEU}_{d,\ell}+\text{BLEU}(v_{k}^{\text{gt}},v_{k}^{\text{pred}})</annotation></semantics></math>;  <span id="algorithm1.4.22.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm1.4.22.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">See Eq. (<a href="#A1.E2" title="In A.3.1 Metrics Details ‣ A.3 Agentic System Evaluation Related Details ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ An Agentic Toolkit for Adaptive Information Extraction from Regulatory Documents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>)</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.23" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.23.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">21</span></span>
              ;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.24" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.24.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">22</span></span>
              <math id="algorithm1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{ROUGE}_{d,\ell}\leftarrow\text{ROUGE}_{d,\ell}+\text{ROUGE-L}(v_{k}^{\text{gt}},v_{k}^{\text{pred}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>ROUGE</mtext><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>ROUGE</mtext><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mtext>ROUGE-L</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi><mtext>gt</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi><mtext>pred</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{ROUGE}_{d,\ell}\leftarrow\text{ROUGE}_{d,\ell}+\text{ROUGE-L}(v_{k}^{\text{gt}},v_{k}^{\text{pred}})</annotation></semantics></math>;  <span id="algorithm1.4.24.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm1.4.24.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">See Eq. (<a href="#A1.E3" title="In A.3.1 Metrics Details ‣ A.3 Agentic System Evaluation Related Details ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ An Agentic Toolkit for Adaptive Information Extraction from Regulatory Documents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>)</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.25" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.25.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">23</span></span>
              ;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.26" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.26.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">24</span></span>
              <math id="algorithm1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\leftarrow\max(|\mathcal{M}_{d,\ell}|,\ 12)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn> 12</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\leftarrow\max(|\mathcal{M}_{d,\ell}|,\ 12)</annotation></semantics></math>;  <span id="algorithm1.4.26.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm1.4.26.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Normalize over matched keys or fixed baseline</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.27" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.27.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">25</span></span>
              <math id="algorithm1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{EM}_{d,\ell}\leftarrow\frac{\text{EM}_{d,\ell}}{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>EM</mtext><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mfrac><msub><mtext>EM</mtext><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mi>Z</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{EM}_{d,\ell}\leftarrow\frac{\text{EM}_{d,\ell}}{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.28" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.28.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">26</span></span>
              <math id="algorithm1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{BLEU}_{d,\ell}\leftarrow\frac{\text{BLEU}_{d,\ell}}{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>BLEU</mtext><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mfrac><msub><mtext>BLEU</mtext><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mi>Z</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{BLEU}_{d,\ell}\leftarrow\frac{\text{BLEU}_{d,\ell}}{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.29" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.29.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">27</span></span>
              <math id="algorithm1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{ROUGE}_{d,\ell}\leftarrow\frac{\text{ROUGE}_{d,\ell}}{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>ROUGE</mtext><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mfrac><msub><mtext>ROUGE</mtext><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mi>Z</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{ROUGE}_{d,\ell}\leftarrow\frac{\text{ROUGE}_{d,\ell}}{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.30" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.30.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">28</span></span>
              <span id="algorithm1.4.30.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <em id="algorithm1.4.30.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{valid}_{d,\ell},\ \text{KeyMatch}_{d,\ell},\ \text{EM}_{d,\ell},\ \text{BLEU}_{d,\ell},\ \text{ROUGE}_{d,\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">valid</mtext><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">KeyMatch</mtext><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">EM</mtext><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">BLEU</mtext><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">ROUGE</mtext><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{valid}_{d,\ell},\ \text{KeyMatch}_{d,\ell},\ \text{EM}_{d,\ell},\ \text{BLEU}_{d,\ell},\ \text{ROUGE}_{d,\ell}</annotation></semantics></math></em>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.3.3 </span>Aggregation of Evaluation Metrics for QA Task</h4>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the QA task, the system is evaluated on its ability to correctly answer a set of natural language questions for each <math id="A1.SS3.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\text{doc},\text{language})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>doc</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext>language</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\text{doc},\text{language})</annotation></semantics></math> pair, as outlined in Algorithm <a href="#algorithm2" title="In A.3.3 Aggregation of Evaluation Metrics for QA Task ‣ A.3 Agentic System Evaluation Related Details ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ An Agentic Toolkit for Adaptive Information Extraction from Regulatory Documents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. Similar to the KVP task, if a ground truth question exists but the system provides no answer, we assign a score of zero for that item across all metrics. This approach avoids discarding samples with missing predictions and ensures that models are fairly penalized for incomplete outputs. Unlike the KVP task, the number of questions may vary per document (see Section <span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_label ltx_ref_self"></span>), so no fixed normalization is applied. Instead, we compute unweighted averages of the value similarity scores across all available question–answer pairs for each document–language combination. These document-level scores are then aggregated to obtain overall averages across the evaluation set.</p>
</div>
<figure id="algorithm2" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="algorithm2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span>QA Evaluation and Aggregation Procedure</figcaption>
<div id="algorithm2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="algorithm2.4.1" class="ltx_listingline">


<span id="algorithm2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input :</span> Ground truth answers <math id="algorithm2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{d,\ell,q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{d,\ell,q}</annotation></semantics></math> and predicted answers <math id="algorithm2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{a}_{d,\ell,q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}_{d,\ell,q}</annotation></semantics></math> for all questions <math id="algorithm2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> in document <math id="algorithm2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> and user language <math id="algorithm2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.2" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output :</span> Per-question scores, document-language averages
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.3" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1</span></span>
              <span id="algorithm2.4.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 1: Merge Predictions with Ground Truth</span>
<span id="algorithm2.4.3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">foreach</span> <em id="algorithm2.4.3.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(d,\ell,q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(d,\ell,q)</annotation></semantics></math> in ground truth</em> <span id="algorithm2.4.3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.4" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">2</span></span>
              <span id="algorithm2.4.4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <em id="algorithm2.4.4.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(d,\ell,q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(d,\ell,q)</annotation></semantics></math> exists in predictions</em> <span id="algorithm2.4.4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.5" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">3</span></span>
              Use predicted answer <math id="algorithm2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{a}_{d,\ell,q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}_{d,\ell,q}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.6" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">4</span></span>
              <span id="algorithm2.4.6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.7" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">5</span></span>
              Set <math id="algorithm2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{a}_{d,\ell,q}\leftarrow\text{empty string}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mtext>empty string</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}_{d,\ell,q}\leftarrow\text{empty string}</annotation></semantics></math> ;  <span id="algorithm2.4.7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm2.4.7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Missing predictions get zero score</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.8" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">6</span></span>
              <span id="algorithm2.4.8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 2: Evaluate Each Question</span>
<span id="algorithm2.4.8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">foreach</span> <em id="algorithm2.4.8.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(d,\ell,q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(d,\ell,q)</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm2.4.8.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.9" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">7</span></span>
              Normalize <math id="algorithm2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{d,\ell,q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{d,\ell,q}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="algorithm2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{a}_{d,\ell,q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}_{d,\ell,q}</annotation></semantics></math> ;  <span id="algorithm2.4.9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm2.4.9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">e.g., lowercasing, stripping punctuation</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.10" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">8</span></span>
              <span id="algorithm2.4.10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <em id="algorithm2.4.10.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{a}_{d,\ell,q}=a_{d,\ell,q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}_{d,\ell,q}=a_{d,\ell,q}</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm2.4.10.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.11" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">9</span></span>
              <math id="algorithm2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{EM}_{d,\ell,q}\leftarrow 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>EM</mtext><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{EM}_{d,\ell,q}\leftarrow 1</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.12" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.12.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">10</span></span>
              <span id="algorithm2.4.12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.13" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.13.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">11</span></span>
              <math id="algorithm2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{EM}_{d,\ell,q}\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>EM</mtext><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{EM}_{d,\ell,q}\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.14" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.14.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">12</span></span>
              <math id="algorithm2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{BLEU}_{d,\ell,q}\leftarrow\text{BLEU}(a_{d,\ell,q},\ \hat{a}_{d,\ell,q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>BLEU</mtext><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext>BLEU</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{BLEU}_{d,\ell,q}\leftarrow\text{BLEU}(a_{d,\ell,q},\ \hat{a}_{d,\ell,q})</annotation></semantics></math> ;  <span id="algorithm2.4.14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm2.4.14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">with smoothing</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.15" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.15.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">13</span></span>
              <math id="algorithm2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{ROUGE}_{d,\ell,q}\leftarrow\text{ROUGE-L}(a_{d,\ell,q},\ \hat{a}_{d,\ell,q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>ROUGE</mtext><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext>ROUGE-L</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{ROUGE}_{d,\ell,q}\leftarrow\text{ROUGE-L}(a_{d,\ell,q},\ \hat{a}_{d,\ell,q})</annotation></semantics></math> ;  <span id="algorithm2.4.15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm2.4.15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">F1 score from LCS</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.16" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.16.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">14</span></span>
              <span id="algorithm2.4.16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 3: Aggregate Document-Language Scores</span>
<span id="algorithm2.4.16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">foreach</span> <em id="algorithm2.4.16.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(d,\ell)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(d,\ell)</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm2.4.16.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.17" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.17.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">15</span></span>
              Let <math id="algorithm2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Q}_{d,\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Q}_{d,\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> be the set of all questions for <math id="algorithm2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(d,\ell)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(d,\ell)</annotation></semantics></math> ;
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.18" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.18.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">16</span></span>
               <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.18.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">17</span></span>
              Compute:

<table id="A1.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{EM}_{d,\ell}^{\text{avg}}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{Q}_{d,\ell}|}\sum_{q}\text{EM}_{d,\ell,q}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mtext>EM</mtext><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mtext>avg</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>q</mi></munder><msub><mtext>EM</mtext><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{EM}_{d,\ell}^{\text{avg}}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{Q}_{d,\ell}|}\sum_{q}\text{EM}_{d,\ell,q}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A1.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{BLEU}_{d,\ell}^{\text{avg}}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{Q}_{d,\ell}|}\sum_{q}\text{BLEU}_{d,\ell,q}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mtext>BLEU</mtext><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mtext>avg</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>q</mi></munder><msub><mtext>BLEU</mtext><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{BLEU}_{d,\ell}^{\text{avg}}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{Q}_{d,\ell}|}\sum_{q}\text{BLEU}_{d,\ell,q}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A1.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{ROUGE}_{d,\ell}^{\text{avg}}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{Q}_{d,\ell}|}\sum_{q}\text{ROUGE}_{d,\ell,q}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mtext>ROUGE</mtext><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mtext>avg</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>q</mi></munder><msub><mtext>ROUGE</mtext><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{ROUGE}_{d,\ell}^{\text{avg}}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{Q}_{d,\ell}|}\sum_{q}\text{ROUGE}_{d,\ell,q}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.19" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.19.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">18</span></span>
              <span id="algorithm2.4.19.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <em id="algorithm2.4.19.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Table of per-question scores, document-language averages</em>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.3.4 </span>Error Logging and Invalid Outputs</h4>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To ensure robustness and traceability in evaluation, all execution failures encountered during agent processing are systematically recorded. These errors may stem from input parsing issues, image extraction failures, model output malformation, or other runtime exceptions. By logging failure metadata such as document name, user language, and error trace, we enable targeted debugging and facilitate quantitative analysis of system limitations.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.SSS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">KVP Task.</span> In the key–value extraction task, errors typically occur at the document level, corrupted PDFs, failed extraction pipelines, or outputs that cannot be parsed into valid JSON structures. Since the agent is required to return a complete JSON structure containing 12 predefined key–value pairs, partial evaluation is not feasible. Even if the process fails midway, the entire output is considered invalid. Rather than discarding these cases from evaluation, we assign zero scores to all metrics. This zero-padding approach ensures consistent treatment across the dataset and prevents artificially inflated averages. To support post-hoc analysis, all failed cases are logged with document metadata and error traces. We also store the raw outputs with validity flags to facilitate deeper investigation of structural errors.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.SSS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">QA Task.</span> For the QA task, each document may contain multiple questions in a given language, and errors are logged at the level of individual question–document–language triples. Failures can arise during PDF-to-image conversion, multi-image model inference, or malformed model outputs (e.g., empty strings or irrelevant text). Unlike KVP, partial evaluation is still possible: if some questions fail, the remaining ones from the same document can still be evaluated. This enables broader coverage even in the presence of localized failures.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">In both tasks, structured error logging plays a critical role in exposing systemic weaknesses and guiding future improvements to the agent’s robustness and reliability across languages and document formats.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS5" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.3.5 </span>Aggregation of Evaluation Metrics for Nested-KVP Task</h4>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The evaluation metrics introduced so far-JSON Validity, Key Match Ratio, and Value Similarity scores such as Exact Match, BLEU, and ROUGE-L ( (<a href="#A1.E2" title="In A.3.1 Metrics Details ‣ A.3 Agentic System Evaluation Related Details ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ An Agentic Toolkit for Adaptive Information Extraction from Regulatory Documents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>),  (<a href="#A1.E1" title="In A.3.1 Metrics Details ‣ A.3 Agentic System Evaluation Related Details ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ An Agentic Toolkit for Adaptive Information Extraction from Regulatory Documents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>),  (<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_label ltx_ref_self"></span>),  (<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_label ltx_ref_self"></span>),  (<a href="#A1.E3" title="In A.3.1 Metrics Details ‣ A.3 Agentic System Evaluation Related Details ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ An Agentic Toolkit for Adaptive Information Extraction from Regulatory Documents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>))-assume a flat structure, where each target corresponds to a single key–value pair. However, in the KVP task, some fields, such as <span id="A1.SS3.SSS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Declared Performance</span>, <span id="A1.SS3.SSS5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Signature</span>, and their German counterparts <span id="A1.SS3.SSS5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Erklärte Leistung</span> and <span id="A1.SS3.SSS5.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Unterschrift</span>, contain structured values encoded as nested JSON objects.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To more accurately evaluate such cases, we extend our framework with a recursive strategy tailored for nested values. As detailed in Algorithm <a href="#algorithm3" title="In A.3.5 Aggregation of Evaluation Metrics for Nested-KVP Task ‣ A.3 Agentic System Evaluation Related Details ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ An Agentic Toolkit for Adaptive Information Extraction from Regulatory Documents" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, the process begins by verifying that the predicted and ground truth values for these keys are valid JSON objects. If valid, each structure is flattened into a set of path–value pairs, where each path is constructed by joining nested keys with a delimiter (e.g., <span id="A1.SS3.SSS5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">"/"</span>), as shown below.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS5.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A1.SS3.SSS5.p3.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="116.02" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 653.15 116.02" width="653.15"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,116.02) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#BF8040;" fill="#BF8040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.49 L 0 111.53 C 0 114.01 2.01 116.02 4.49 116.02 L 648.66 116.02 C 651.14 116.02 653.15 114.01 653.15 111.53 L 653.15 4.49 C 653.15 2.01 651.14 0 648.66 0 L 4.49 0 C 2.01 0 0 2.01 0 4.49 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFF9F2;" fill="#FFF9F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.55 4.49 L 0.55 94.74 L 652.6 94.74 L 652.6 4.49 C 652.6 2.32 650.83 0.55 648.66 0.55 L 4.49 0.55 C 2.32 0.55 0.55 2.32 0.55 4.49 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.24 101.93)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:44.28em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="612.71"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.SS3.SSS5.p3.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:44.28em;">
